1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:02,697
Your Jenkins server will fail one day.

2
00:00:03,247 --> 00:00:07,663
A disk fills up. An upgrade goes wrong. Someone deletes the wrong job.

3
00:00:08,213 --> 00:00:11,971
Then there is only one question: how fast can you get it back?

4
00:00:11,971 --> 00:00:14,819
A team with a tested backup answers in minutes.

5
00:00:14,819 --> 00:00:17,001
A team without one answers in weeks,

6
00:00:17,001 --> 00:00:17,728
from memory.

7
00:00:18,278 --> 00:00:20,760
Today you do all of it in real Jenkins.

8
00:00:20,760 --> 00:00:21,714
You back it up,

9
00:00:21,714 --> 00:00:22,287
break it,

10
00:00:22,287 --> 00:00:22,987
restore it,

11
00:00:22,987 --> 00:00:23,941
and upgrade it.

12
00:00:23,941 --> 00:00:25,659
And you fix a failed build.

13
00:00:27,209 --> 00:00:28,638
Here is what to expect.

14
00:00:29,188 --> 00:00:33,220
One: the four ideas. Backup, restore, upgrade, and triage.

15
00:00:33,770 --> 00:00:37,226
Two: a picture of Jenkins home, and what goes in a backup.

16
00:00:37,776 --> 00:00:39,041
Three: a live demo,

17
00:00:39,041 --> 00:00:40,306
in a real terminal,

18
00:00:40,306 --> 00:00:42,436
and in the real Jenkins screens.

19
00:00:42,436 --> 00:00:43,168
We back up,

20
00:00:43,168 --> 00:00:44,233
we delete a job,

21
00:00:44,233 --> 00:00:45,164
we restore it,

22
00:00:45,164 --> 00:00:46,629
we fix a broken build,

23
00:00:46,629 --> 00:00:49,424
and we upgrade Jenkins to a newer version.

24
00:00:49,974 --> 00:00:52,790
Four: the common mistakes, and where to find the lab.

25
00:00:53,340 --> 00:00:56,178
This is objective nine of the Jenkins domain.

26
00:00:57,728 --> 00:00:58,944
Four words to know.

27
00:00:59,494 --> 00:01:02,438
Backup: a copy of Jenkins home, kept somewhere else.

28
00:01:02,988 --> 00:01:06,785
Restore: bring back one job, or the whole server, from that copy.

29
00:01:07,335 --> 00:01:10,407
Upgrade: swap the war file, and keep the home folder.

30
00:01:10,957 --> 00:01:14,456
Triage: find which stage failed, then read the first error.

31
00:01:15,006 --> 00:01:19,550
Backup, restore, upgrade, triage. Practise all four, before you need them.

32
00:01:21,100 --> 00:01:26,732
Here is Jenkins home, in one picture. Everything Jenkins knows lives in this one folder.

33
00:01:27,282 --> 00:01:30,903
The file config.xml holds the main settings.

34
00:01:30,903 --> 00:01:33,220
The folder jobs holds every job,

35
00:01:33,220 --> 00:01:34,813
and its build history.

36
00:01:35,363 --> 00:01:38,385
The folder plugins holds the installed plugins.

37
00:01:38,385 --> 00:01:42,500
The folder secrets holds the keys that protect your credentials.

38
00:01:42,500 --> 00:01:44,621
Guard the backup like a password.

39
00:01:45,171 --> 00:01:47,968
The folders workspace and caches are different.

40
00:01:47,968 --> 00:01:49,277
Jenkins rebuilds them,

41
00:01:49,277 --> 00:01:50,526
so we leave them out.

42
00:01:51,076 --> 00:01:53,082
The war file is Jenkins itself.

43
00:01:53,082 --> 00:01:55,216
It lives outside the home folder.

44
00:01:55,216 --> 00:01:57,804
That is why an upgrade replaces the war,

45
00:01:57,804 --> 00:01:59,033
and keeps the home.

46
00:01:59,583 --> 00:02:02,762
Backup the home. Swap the war. That is the whole idea.

47
00:02:04,312 --> 00:02:05,298
A real Jenkins,

48
00:02:05,298 --> 00:02:06,548
signed in as admin.

49
00:02:06,548 --> 00:02:08,652
It has been working for a while.

50
00:02:08,652 --> 00:02:09,178
One job,

51
00:02:09,178 --> 00:02:10,296
CloudCart build,

52
00:02:10,296 --> 00:02:11,743
with two green builds.

53
00:02:11,743 --> 00:02:14,899
Everything it knows lives in one folder on disk,

54
00:02:14,899 --> 00:02:16,214
called Jenkins home.

55
00:02:16,214 --> 00:02:17,529
Today we back it up,

56
00:02:17,529 --> 00:02:18,121
break it,

57
00:02:18,121 --> 00:02:18,844
restore it,

58
00:02:18,844 --> 00:02:19,568
upgrade it,

59
00:02:19,568 --> 00:02:21,080
and fix a failed build.

60
00:02:21,630 --> 00:02:22,029
First,

61
00:02:22,029 --> 00:02:22,761
the backup.

62
00:02:22,761 --> 00:02:25,556
This is a terminal on the Jenkins machine.

63
00:02:25,556 --> 00:02:28,151
Jenkins keeps everything in one folder,

64
00:02:28,151 --> 00:02:30,347
and its path is in this variable.

65
00:02:30,347 --> 00:02:31,079
Here it is.

66
00:02:31,079 --> 00:02:32,809
Now the folders inside it.

67
00:02:33,359 --> 00:02:34,645
Four things matter.

68
00:02:34,645 --> 00:02:36,405
The file config.xml,

69
00:02:36,405 --> 00:02:37,623
the main settings.

70
00:02:37,623 --> 00:02:38,706
The folder jobs,

71
00:02:38,706 --> 00:02:40,872
every job and its build history.

72
00:02:40,872 --> 00:02:42,158
The folder plugins,

73
00:02:42,158 --> 00:02:43,647
the installed plugins.

74
00:02:43,647 --> 00:02:45,204
And the folder secrets,

75
00:02:45,204 --> 00:02:47,844
the keys that protect your credentials.

76
00:02:47,844 --> 00:02:50,281
Workspace and caches can be rebuilt,

77
00:02:50,281 --> 00:02:51,364
so we skip them.

78
00:02:51,914 --> 00:02:53,475
Now the backup itself.

79
00:02:53,475 --> 00:02:54,823
The command is tar.

80
00:02:54,823 --> 00:02:56,242
czf means: create,

81
00:02:56,242 --> 00:02:56,881
compress,

82
00:02:56,881 --> 00:02:58,513
and write to this file.

83
00:02:58,513 --> 00:03:01,635
We save it in a folder outside Jenkins home,

84
00:03:01,635 --> 00:03:04,757
and we exclude the workspace and the caches.

85
00:03:05,307 --> 00:03:06,784
It takes a few seconds,

86
00:03:06,784 --> 00:03:08,454
because plugins are large.

87
00:03:08,454 --> 00:03:09,353
While it runs,

88
00:03:09,353 --> 00:03:11,600
remember the first rule of backups.

89
00:03:11,600 --> 00:03:14,169
A copy on the same disk is not a backup.

90
00:03:14,169 --> 00:03:15,711
Send it to another disk,

91
00:03:15,711 --> 00:03:16,867
or another server,

92
00:03:16,867 --> 00:03:17,637
every night.

93
00:03:23,487 --> 00:03:28,415
Check the result. List the backup folder. The archive is there, and this is its size.

94
00:03:28,965 --> 00:03:29,262
Now,

95
00:03:29,262 --> 00:03:30,226
the disaster.

96
00:03:30,226 --> 00:03:32,820
Someone deletes the job by mistake.

97
00:03:32,820 --> 00:03:33,636
In Jenkins,

98
00:03:33,636 --> 00:03:35,267
open CloudCart build.

99
00:03:35,267 --> 00:03:36,157
On the left,

100
00:03:36,157 --> 00:03:37,862
choose Delete Pipeline.

101
00:03:37,862 --> 00:03:39,419
And confirm with Yes.

102
00:03:39,969 --> 00:03:43,958
The dashboard is empty. The job is gone, and so is its history.

103
00:03:44,508 --> 00:03:45,660
Now the restore.

104
00:03:45,660 --> 00:03:47,531
We only need that one job.

105
00:03:47,531 --> 00:03:51,059
Tar can extract a single folder from the archive.

106
00:03:51,059 --> 00:03:53,650
Extract jobs slash CloudCart build,

107
00:03:53,650 --> 00:03:54,946
into Jenkins home.

108
00:03:54,946 --> 00:03:56,817
Then list the jobs folder.

109
00:03:57,367 --> 00:03:59,602
But Jenkins still shows nothing.

110
00:03:59,602 --> 00:04:01,558
It keeps its jobs in memory.

111
00:04:01,558 --> 00:04:02,955
Open Manage Jenkins,

112
00:04:02,955 --> 00:04:05,889
and choose Reload Configuration from Disk.

113
00:04:05,889 --> 00:04:06,797
Then confirm.

114
00:04:10,747 --> 00:04:12,162
Back to the dashboard.

115
00:04:12,162 --> 00:04:13,191
The job is back,

116
00:04:13,191 --> 00:04:14,155
with build one,

117
00:04:14,155 --> 00:04:15,056
and build two.

118
00:04:15,056 --> 00:04:18,786
Remember: a backup you have never restored is only a hope.

119
00:04:18,786 --> 00:04:19,493
Test yours.

120
00:04:20,043 --> 00:04:30,283
Now a build that fails. New Item, named broken build, of type Pipeline. Then OK.

121
00:04:32,733 --> 00:04:34,030
Here is the script.

122
00:04:34,030 --> 00:04:35,121
Read it with me.

123
00:04:35,121 --> 00:04:35,803
One stage,

124
00:04:35,803 --> 00:04:36,213
Build.

125
00:04:36,213 --> 00:04:37,987
It gets the code from git.

126
00:04:37,987 --> 00:04:39,283
Then it runs Maven,

127
00:04:39,283 --> 00:04:41,193
with the goal clean package.

128
00:04:41,193 --> 00:04:42,694
Except in this script,

129
00:04:42,694 --> 00:04:43,786
there is a typo.

130
00:04:43,786 --> 00:04:46,515
Package is spelled without the letter A.

131
00:04:47,065 --> 00:04:49,731
Save, and Build Now. Then open the console.

132
00:04:56,481 --> 00:04:56,778
Red.

133
00:04:56,778 --> 00:04:58,487
Triage has three steps.

134
00:04:58,487 --> 00:05:00,269
One: which stage failed?

135
00:05:00,269 --> 00:05:01,977
Open Pipeline Overview.

136
00:05:01,977 --> 00:05:03,685
The Build stage is red.

137
00:05:03,685 --> 00:05:06,730
Two: find the first error in the console,

138
00:05:06,730 --> 00:05:07,993
not the last one.

139
00:05:07,993 --> 00:05:09,107
Three: read it.

140
00:05:09,107 --> 00:05:10,889
Unknown lifecycle phase,

141
00:05:10,889 --> 00:05:11,409
packge.

142
00:05:11,409 --> 00:05:12,375
It is a typo.

143
00:05:12,925 --> 00:05:18,813
Fix the script. Open Configure, and go to the Pipeline section.

144
00:05:19,363 --> 00:05:20,535
Retype the script.

145
00:05:20,535 --> 00:05:22,944
The only change is one word: package,

146
00:05:22,944 --> 00:05:24,117
with the letter A.

147
00:05:24,117 --> 00:05:26,135
Everything else stays the same.

148
00:05:26,135 --> 00:05:26,787
Then Save.

149
00:05:31,037 --> 00:05:36,391
Build Now again. Maven runs, and the console ends with Finished: success. Green.

150
00:05:39,641 --> 00:05:41,061
Now the upgrade drill.

151
00:05:41,061 --> 00:05:43,321
This second Jenkins is a throwaway,

152
00:05:43,321 --> 00:05:44,354
on another port.

153
00:05:44,354 --> 00:05:50,163
Look at the bottom right of the page: the version is two point five five five point three.

154
00:05:50,163 --> 00:05:51,132
It has one job,

155
00:05:51,132 --> 00:05:52,100
with one build.

156
00:05:52,650 --> 00:05:54,260
Rule one: back up first.

157
00:05:54,260 --> 00:05:55,937
Go to the upgrade folder,

158
00:05:55,937 --> 00:05:57,414
and stop this Jenkins.

159
00:05:57,414 --> 00:05:59,024
Archive its home folder.

160
00:05:59,024 --> 00:06:01,909
Then point the Jenkins home variable at it.

161
00:06:02,459 --> 00:06:04,305
Rule two: swap the war file.

162
00:06:04,305 --> 00:06:06,019
The war is Jenkins itself.

163
00:06:06,019 --> 00:06:07,140
Keep the old one,

164
00:06:07,140 --> 00:06:08,789
in case you must go back.

165
00:06:08,789 --> 00:06:10,108
Copy the new one in.

166
00:06:10,108 --> 00:06:11,888
And ask it for its version.

167
00:06:12,438 --> 00:06:13,817
Now start Jenkins again,

168
00:06:13,817 --> 00:06:15,195
on the same home folder.

169
00:06:15,195 --> 00:06:17,665
The first start after an upgrade is slower,

170
00:06:17,665 --> 00:06:21,571
because Jenkins checks every job and plugin against the new version.

171
00:06:21,571 --> 00:06:22,490
While it starts,

172
00:06:22,490 --> 00:06:24,960
here is the checklist for after an upgrade.

173
00:06:24,960 --> 00:06:26,453
The version in the footer.

174
00:06:26,453 --> 00:06:26,970
The jobs,

175
00:06:26,970 --> 00:06:28,004
and their history.

176
00:06:28,004 --> 00:06:28,981
The plugins page,

177
00:06:28,981 --> 00:06:29,727
for warnings.

178
00:06:29,727 --> 00:06:30,819
And one test build.

179
00:06:30,819 --> 00:06:32,025
If anything is wrong,

180
00:06:32,025 --> 00:06:33,691
the way back is simple: stop,

181
00:06:33,691 --> 00:06:34,897
put the old war back,

182
00:06:34,897 --> 00:06:36,218
and restore the backup.

183
00:06:36,218 --> 00:06:37,654
That is why we kept both.

184
00:06:45,404 --> 00:06:46,463
Reload the page.

185
00:06:46,463 --> 00:06:50,171
The footer now says two point five eight zero point two.

186
00:06:50,171 --> 00:06:52,488
The job demo upgrade is still here,

187
00:06:52,488 --> 00:06:53,746
with its old build.

188
00:06:53,746 --> 00:06:55,004
Run one test build.

189
00:07:03,154 --> 00:07:07,421
Green. That is a safe upgrade: back up, swap the war, check, and test.

190
00:07:08,971 --> 00:07:10,123
Five mistakes.

191
00:07:10,673 --> 00:07:14,854
One: the backup sits on the same disk. When the disk dies, both die.

192
00:07:15,404 --> 00:07:20,247
Two: a backup nobody has restored. Practise a restore, before the bad day.

193
00:07:20,797 --> 00:07:25,256
Three: upgrading with no backup. Always back up first, and keep the old war.

194
00:07:25,806 --> 00:07:31,054
Four: upgrading Jenkins and every plugin on the same day. Change one thing at a time.

195
00:07:31,604 --> 00:07:36,126
Five: reading the last error. Read the first error, it is usually the cause.

196
00:07:37,676 --> 00:07:40,471
Where to find the lab. Pause here, and write it down.

197
00:07:41,021 --> 00:07:42,485
One: the repository,

198
00:07:42,485 --> 00:07:46,805
GitHub dot com slash it dash waves slash dev ops dash A I,

199
00:07:46,805 --> 00:07:49,149
in the folder academy slash lab.

200
00:07:49,699 --> 00:07:55,757
Two: the files, lab162 dot S H, and shortcuts one sixty-two dot S H.

201
00:07:56,307 --> 00:08:01,769
Three: install it, with sudo install, into slash user slash local slash S bin.

202
00:08:02,319 --> 00:08:07,844
Four: load the short names, with source shortcuts one sixty-two dot S H. Then lab up.

203
00:08:08,394 --> 00:08:10,766
Five: lab backup makes the archive.

204
00:08:10,766 --> 00:08:12,935
Lab restore brings one job back.

205
00:08:12,935 --> 00:08:17,205
Lab old starts the throwaway old Jenkins for the upgrade drill.

206
00:08:17,755 --> 00:08:21,402
Six: you need the Jenkins from lesson one fifty-five,

207
00:08:21,402 --> 00:08:22,021
and Java.

208
00:08:22,021 --> 00:08:24,155
Lab down removes the lab files.

209
00:08:24,705 --> 00:08:26,347
The link is in the description.

210
00:08:27,897 --> 00:08:29,668
Your turn, on your own machine.

211
00:08:30,218 --> 00:08:33,098
One: lab up, and make a backup with lab backup.

212
00:08:33,648 --> 00:08:36,720
Two: delete a job, and restore it from the archive.

213
00:08:37,270 --> 00:08:40,704
Three: break a pipeline on purpose, and find the first error.

214
00:08:41,254 --> 00:08:44,582
Four: start the throwaway old Jenkins, and upgrade it.

215
00:08:45,132 --> 00:08:49,548
Five: check the version, the job, and run one test build. Then lab down.

216
00:08:50,098 --> 00:08:51,933
Pause the video, and begin now.

217
00:09:07,483 --> 00:09:08,358
Quick check.

218
00:09:08,908 --> 00:09:10,721
What goes into a Jenkins backup?

219
00:09:11,271 --> 00:09:13,618
Why is a backup on the same disk not enough?

220
00:09:14,168 --> 00:09:16,301
How do you bring back one deleted job?

221
00:09:16,851 --> 00:09:18,963
What do you read first, in a failed build?

222
00:09:19,513 --> 00:09:25,593
Objective covered: MC17-O09. Backup, upgrade and troubleshooting.

223
00:09:26,143 --> 00:09:28,212
Pause the video, and answer out loud.

224
00:09:38,762 --> 00:09:43,712
Next: the Jenkins mastery lesson, a full scenario you can verify yourself.

225
00:09:44,262 --> 00:09:47,590
